// A Whisper of Doom (D10), p.22-23.
(
    name: "Whisper of Doom",
    die: D10,
    entries: [
        (1, 1, (title: "The Silent Saint", text: "You heard a tale of a hermit who cannot hear the Choir's hymn. They are a void in the divine symphony. Is their silence a blessing, a cure, or a different kind of damnation? You seek them as a beacon of hope, but the Choir hunts this blasphemous silence relentlessly, and the Flesh is drawn to such anomalies.")),
        (2, 2, (title: "The Heretical Chant", text: "A mad scholar's journal spoke of a \"Gnostic Counter-Psalm\", a sequence of notes and discordant rites that can shatter a Penitent's faith and body. The map to its hiding place is incomplete, and the ritual is said to require a sacrifice of voice, memory, or flesh. You seek to weaponize it, knowing the performance might unmake you just as surely as it unmakes the enemy.")),
        (3, 3, (title: "Unholy Ground", text: "There is a rumor of a valley, a forgotten abbey, or a hidden island that remains untouched by both Choir and Flesh—a pocket of the old world. You seek this sanctuary as a place to live, not just survive. But if it exists, it is a prize both apocalypses would kill to claim, and the path to it is a pilgrimage through hell.")),
        (4, 4, (title: "The First Apostate", text: "You hunt for the first soul who chose the Flesh over the Choir. They say this individual carved out their own tongue with an obsidian shard and still lives, a sentient tumor deep within the Flesh's territory. They may hold the secret to resisting the Choir without losing oneself entirely, but their \"salvation\" is a horror all its own.")),
        (5, 5, (title: "The Child of the Twin Apocalypses", text: "A blasphemous whisper tells of a child born of a Choir Penitent and a Flesh Apostate. A creature of both song and sinew, harmony and hunger. Is this being the key to ending the war, a bridge between the two horrors, or the final verse that will complete their apocalyptic song? You seek this abomination, knowing it is hunted by everyone and its very existence is a paradox that could unravel reality.")),
        (6, 6, (title: "The Cistern of Old Prayers", text: "Rumors speak of a place where the Choir's song is weakest: a vast, subterranean cistern beneath a ruined city where the echoes of a million prayers still linger. They say these old prayers confuse the hymn, offering a brief respite. You seek it as a place to think, to plan, but what happens when the Choir decides to silence those old prayers for good?")),
        (7, 7, (title: "The Blasphemous Name", text: "The Flesh That Feeds is mindless, but an ancient pagan text you found claims it was not always so. It once had a name, and to speak that name is to give it a mind once more. Could this grant you a moment's control, a chance to bargain, or would it simply turn its infinite, mindless hunger into a focused, malevolent intellect?")),
        (8, 8, (title: "The Papal Testament", text: "Before Pope Sylvester II became the Choir's mouthpiece, he wrote a final, secret encyclical condemning the \"angels\" and detailing a potential weakness. The letter was smuggled out of Rome but never reached its destination. You search for this last testament of the true Church, a document that could turn the faithful against their heavenly tormentors.")),
        (9, 9, (title: "The Black Bell", text: "A smith's ledger describes a bell forged with iron from a fallen star. When rung, it produces no sound, only a wave of profound, crushing silence that can reportedly shatter the resolve of Penitents and drive away the Flesh's spawn. The bell is said to be lost in a city that now serves as a battlefield for the War of the Millennium.")),
        (10, 10, (title: "The Divine Conductor", text: "You believe the Choir's song originates from a single point, a \"Maestro\" angel conducting the symphony of the end. You have a clue (a star-chart, a prophetic dream, a Penitent's dying whisper) that points to its location. Your quest is simple and impossible: to travel to the heart of the Choir's power and kill the conductor of the apocalypse.")),
    ],
)
